{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1457486-questions-about-show-of-power-exploit","id":1457486,"title":"Questions about Show of Power exploit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-23T09:50:35-07:00","id":1457486,"title":"Questions about Show of Power exploit","content":"How long can a demon mimic the powers demonstrated or shown in front of them by another monster type? Along with that, if the power copied is used in front of monsters not of that type (using some Mage spell in front of Sin Eaters) do they even get a chance to note it's chicanery? The rule for roll noticing is the highest wits + Supernatural tolerance of that creature type. But if there is no mage there...? And i am slightly confused on innate/non rolled abilities. If a demon witnesses a werewolf regenerate, does that mean activating the power would let the demon regenerate that turn like a uratha? Or shifting forms, would that mean the demon could also shift, but since its a copy...would you just have your normal stats with a giant uratha shape body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T06:55:30-07:00","id":1466933,"title":"","content":"I'll do my best to answer your questions but overall show of power does have some flaws in how it's written.<br /> <br /> 1) as written there is no limitation to how recently a demon witnessed the ability, only that they have witnessed the ability they wish to mimic.<br /> 2) the resistance roll is specific to being witnessed by one the power is from. If there is none of that type you roll to activate but it isn't contested.<br /> 3) for abilities that are not a single action, such as werewolf innate regeneration, show of power lasts a scene. As for if you were mimicking shapeshifting, you'd mimic that ability (ie stat changes) and not only have it be cosmetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where show of power is made complicated is edge cases where an ability doesn't rely on multiple successes for a scale effect, as show of power only acts as if you got a single success, such as a mage's spell which only needs a single success to work.<br /> <br /> A common house rules I've seen people implement to try to rein show of power in is to have it be able to &quot;record&quot; only a set number of abilities at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T08:33:40-08:00","id":1467359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1457486-questions-about-show-of-power-exploit?p=1466933#post1466933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll do my best to answer your questions but overall show of power does have some flaws in how it's written.<br /> <br /> 1) as written there is no limitation to how recently a demon witnessed the ability, only that they have witnessed the ability they wish to mimic.<br /> 2) the resistance roll is specific to being witnessed by one the power is from. If there is none of that type you roll to activate but it isn't contested.<br /> 3) for abilities that are not a single action, such as werewolf innate regeneration, show of power lasts a scene. As for if you were mimicking shapeshifting, you'd mimic that ability (ie stat changes) and not only have it be cosmetic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where show of power is made complicated is edge cases where an ability doesn't rely on multiple successes for a scale effect, as show of power only acts as if you got a single success, such as a mage's spell which only needs a single success to work.<br /> <br /> A common house rules I've seen people implement to try to rein show of power in is to have it be able to &quot;record&quot; only a set number of abilities at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with Mr.F.I.X. on the explanation. Yes, this makes Show of Power pretty broken. Especially once you get into Gadget creation.<br /> <br /> Another take I've been thinking about is integrating it into the Legend system, similar to how Persistent Legend does. Still has some bugs, though, mechanically speaking.<br /> <br /> Though... an Ember family with Show of Power as their Exploit would make a <i>great</i> Hunter group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}